--   **The backward states.**
--
--   The following holds (Lean statement, in the scope of module `Solutions.J6SegJPre4`):
--
--   ```lean
--   theorem J6Seg.JK.bwdS_eq (hsort : L.Pairwise (· < ·)) (Y : ℕ → ℤ) : ∀ j ≤ L.length,
--       bwdS P (bsOf P L mw c A) (accF (P := P) (S := bandS mw c) (L := L) (A := A) (b := Y)
--         L.length) j =
--         (accZ P (bandS mw c) L A Y (L.length - j),
--           accB P (bandS mw c) L A Y (flOf L (c ≤ ·)) (L.length - j))
--   ```
--
--   **Context.** `J` kernel precondition (JPre), part 4: the intermediates of the kernel in closed form
--
--   For the streams `fsOf`/`bsOf` of a sorted line `L` (pattern `bandS mw c`, border `c ≤ ·`) and an
--   input `v` (`|L| ≤ |v|`), with the right-hand side `bv L v` (`bv (L_r) = v_r`):
--
--   * `fA_eq`: the forward accumulator after `r` rows is `accF r = [bt_{r-1}, …, bt_0]`;
--   * `bwdS_eq`: the backward state after `j` records is `(accZ (m-j), accB (m-j))` (the solution
--     values `z_{m-j}, …, z_{m-1}` and their border part);
--   * the shapes of the streams (`fsOf_getElem_length`, `bsOf_getElem`, `WbOf_le`,
--     `czOf_length`, `flOf_01`).
